From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Builder <builder@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: phy_meson_usb: program U2P_R0 during aml init

NOT VERIFIED ON HARDWARE. This is derived from the 5.15 vendor driver by
source comparison. No board has booted a kernel carrying it. USB2 does not
initialise on 6.12 today, so a failure here is indistinguishable from the
present state -- which is the point: it is a cheap thing to try, not a
diagnosis.

Both USB2 PHYs fail init on 6.12 with

    wait for ready timeout.
    meson_usb2phy_s7d_set_pll set pll failed, val:0x0f549540
    phy init failed --> -110

The return path is worth stating exactly, because the log misleads. In
meson_u2phy_aml_init() the wait_ready failure is logged and then discarded:
ret is immediately overwritten by priv->set_pll(). So -110 is returned by
set_pll, on a phy that had already failed to report ready. The PLL message
is downstream by construction.

What is missing is U2P_R0. On a cold init nothing in phy_meson_usb writes
it. Every writel to ->r0 in the directory sits inside one of the two mode
setters, meson_u2phy_legacy_set_mode() and meson_u2phy_set_mode(). s7d binds
the latter as priv->set_mode (socs/phy-meson-s7d-usb.c:133), and its only
call sites are guarded by

    if (phy->suspend_flag && phy->current_mode != 0)

current_mode is zero out of the kzalloc() in meson_aml_u2phy_parse(), so
the guard is false and the call does not run. That holds whatever the value
0 denotes in enum meson_uphy_mode. usbphy1's u2p@0 has no phy-otg property,
so no otg helper runs for it at all; usbphy0 has one, but its
MESON_USB_MODE_HOST case only performs a role switch into controller code
and never reaches u2phy_ops->set_mode -- only the OTG case does.

The 5.15 driver that drives this same hardware on this board does program
it. In amlogic_crg_drd_usb2_init_v0(), at line 403 of
drivers/usb/crgdrdphy/phy-aml-crg-drd-usb2.c and reached from compatible
"amlogic, amlogic-crg-drd-usb2" via aml_phy_v0_data, the order is:

    set the phy_reset_level bits          (== hold_reset(true) here)
    amlogic_crg_drd_usbphy_reset()        (== meson_u2phy_usb_reset())
    read U2P_R0, set POR, and when not resuming host_device, IDPULLUP0
        and DRVVBUS0; write it back
    usleep_range(9, 10)
    amlogic_crg_drd_usbphy_reset_phycfg()
    usleep_range(49, 50)
    trim calibration, clear phy_cfg+0x54 bit 2, poll phy_rdy
    set_usb_pll, set_trim_initvalue

so U2P_R0 is established before the config reset is pulsed. 6.12 pulses
that reset having never established it. This patch puts the same
read-modify-write in the same place, immediately before the call to
meson_u2phy_reset_phycfg().

Three notes on how faithful the transcription is:

- The 5.15 guard "if (phy->suspend_flag == 0)" is not carried over. The two
  drivers use suspend_flag with opposite polarity: in 5.15 probe sets it to
  0 and it means "not resuming", so the host bits are written on a cold
  init; here meson_aml_u2phy_parse() sets it to 1 and meson_u2phy_aml_init()
  returns early when it is 0, so it is always 1 at this point. Transcribing
  the condition literally would set POR and skip precisely the three bits
  that are absent.

- POR is left asserted, because init_v0 leaves it asserted. 5.15 clears POR
  elsewhere -- in amlogic_crg_drd_usb2_phy_set_mode(), which only the v1
  init calls, in the gadget init amlogic_crg_device_usb2_init_v0(), and in
  the crg-otg driver's set_mode(). None of those is on the v0 host path this
  board takes at init. Asserting POR is not a change on this board in any
  case: at bootloader handover U2P_R0 reads 0x0a on usbphy0 and 0x0b on
  usbphy1, both with POR already set, and the driver never clears it.

- host_device is set unconditionally, as the 5.15 host init does. 5.15 keeps
  a separate gadget init that writes host_device = 0; 6.12 has one shared
  init, so the host form is taken here. Both ports on this board are host
  (u2p@0 controller-type = <1>). This is a build for this board, not a
  general-purpose change.

The read-modify-write matters and a constant store would be wrong: the two
PHYs arrive from the bootloader with different U2P_R0 values, so the other
bits in the register are per-port state that must be preserved.

What this does not address: reading U2P_R0 back after boot is the only way
to tell whether the write lands and survives the reset pulse, and the 6.12
image has # CONFIG_DEVMEM is not set, so that read has to come from the
U-Boot prompt over serial. docs/task/BUG-010.md carries the procedure.
---
--- a/common_drivers/drivers/usb/phy_meson_usb/phy-meson-aml-usb2-com.c
+++ b/common_drivers/drivers/usb/phy_meson_usb/phy-meson-aml-usb2-com.c
@@ -782,6 +782,7 @@ int meson_u2phy_u3drdu2o_set(struct amlogic_usb_v2 *phy, bool on)
 
 int meson_u2phy_aml_init(struct amlogic_usb_v2 *phy, struct meson_u2phy_priv *priv)
 {
+	union u2p_r0_v2 reg0;
 	int ret;
 
 	if (!phy->suspend_flag) {
@@ -815,6 +816,32 @@ int meson_u2phy_aml_init(struct amlogic_usb_v2 *phy, struct meson_u2phy_priv *pr
 	if (phy->suspend_flag && phy->current_mode != 0)
 		priv->set_mode(phy, phy->current_mode);
 
+	/*
+	 * Establish U2P_R0 before the phy config reset below, mirroring
+	 * amlogic_crg_drd_usb2_init_v0() in the 5.15 crgdrdphy driver, which
+	 * drives this hardware with working USB on this board. Nothing here
+	 * writes U2P_R0 on a cold init: the only writer is priv->set_mode(),
+	 * and the call above is guarded on current_mode, which is zero out of
+	 * the allocator -- so the phy goes through the reset pulse with
+	 * host_device, IDPULLUP0 and DRVVBUS0 clear.
+	 *
+	 * The 5.15 write is guarded by "suspend_flag == 0" and that condition
+	 * is deliberately not transcribed: the two drivers use suspend_flag
+	 * with opposite polarity. There it means "not resuming"; here it means
+	 * "init pending" and is always 1 at this point, since this function
+	 * returns early above when it is 0. Copying the condition would skip
+	 * exactly the bits that are missing.
+	 *
+	 * POR is left set, as init_v0 leaves it set. It is already set at
+	 * bootloader handover on this board, so this does not change it.
+	 */
+	reg0.d32 = readl(&phy->u2p_aml_regs[0]->r0);
+	reg0.b.POR = 1;
+	reg0.b.host_device = 1;
+	reg0.b.IDPULLUP0 = 1;
+	reg0.b.DRVVBUS0 = 1;
+	writel(reg0.d32, &phy->u2p_aml_regs[0]->r0);
+
 	usleep_range(50, 100);
 	meson_u2phy_reset_phycfg(phy);
 	usleep_range(50, 100);
-- 
2.43.0
